  "query_preview": "..  (Thursday through Next Tuesday)\nIssued at 213 PM CDT Tue Jun 16 2026\n\nWith the active weather day ahead tomorrow, the focus of today's \ndiscussion will remain on tomorrow's wind and thunderstorm \npotential. However, there is another potential for showers and \nthunderstorms Sunday and Monday worth discussing, with increasing \nconfidence that parts of the region will see another round of heavy \nrainfall. The synoptic pattern will remain relatively stationary \nwith a longwave trough across the eastern US and shortwaves pivoting \naround its periphery throughout the week. While tomorrow's cold \nfront will push moisture and instability south for several days, \neventually this will begin to return north and back into our region, \nsetting the stage for more rain. Anomalously high PWAT values \n(90th percentile ensemble means) and the potential for multiple \nrounds of rain support this, and LREF probabilities suggest a \nreasonable potential (20-50%) for 2 inches of rain or more. There \nremain considerable differences in the timing and placement of \nthis rain, but this will need to be closely monitored.\n\nBRC",
